# never: the game. The cartridge belongs in roms/ - the path is part of the
# interface, the bytes are not, and git history cannot cleanly un-ship a ROM.
*.nes
*.zip

# Run artefacts ARE tracked, because they are the evidence:
#   logs/*.inputs.txt   the input log of a run - the run itself
#   logs/*.bk2          the exported movie
#   logs/segments/*.json  what the search found for each segment
#   states/*.State      the bookmarks the search searched from
# Caveat: a BizHawk .State only loads in the exact BizHawk build that wrote it,
# so these are pinned to 2.11.1 like everything else here.

# What stays out is the raw emulator stdout: ~100 KB of "Read a zipstate" and
# absolute paths, which says nothing a reader does not already have.
logs/*.log

# Event checkpoints (issue #4): the INDEX is tracked, the BLOBS are not.
#
#   logs/*.checkpoints.json      tracked - what was acquired, at what frame, under
#                                 which route, on which cartridge. ~10 KB for a whole
#                                 run, and it is the provenance record.
#   logs/checkpoints/*_ev*.json  not tracked
#   states/*_ev*.State           not tracked
#
# Why the split: each checkpoint is a 17.9 KB savestate PLUS a JSON carrying the whole
# input prefix that produced it, and the prefix grows with the frame number - so a
# late checkpoint is a few hundred KB of mostly-empty lines. Thirty of those per
# route, times several routes, is megabytes in git history that cannot be cleanly
# undone, for a file that is regenerable by re-running. Disk is cheap; history is
# not. Resuming still works, because "start again from there" only ever needed the
# file on disk.
#
# Note the savestates in states/*.State ARE tracked, because those are the bookmarks
# the searches ran from and the search log refers to them by name.
logs/checkpoints/*_ev*.json
states/*_ev*.State
logs/**/*.log
logs/*.prev.log
# Video dumps are large and regenerable from the .bk2. Screenshots under shots/
# ARE tracked - they are the visual record of what each run actually reached -
# but the global *.png below still keeps every other PNG out of the repository.
video/
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.wav
*.m4a
*.png
!shots/*.png
# the bridge's port file, rewritten on every launch
.bridge_port
youtube/capture/
youtube/clips/
youtube/clips_v3/
youtube/out/
youtube/out_v3/
youtube/voice/
youtube/final/
youtube/check/
youtube/sheets/
# Screenshots taken with a *patched* cartridge. They are of somebody else's
# mod, not of this project's runs, and none of them are evidence for anything the
# stock run does not already show. Keep them out; the patched ROMs themselves
# belong in /tmp.
shots/automap_*.png
shots/mapwin_*.png
shots/hacked_*.png

# third-party disassembly: linked from the README, not redistributed
tools/disasm/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
